\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Layer\nobreakspace  {}2 data flow. The GPU reduction pass aggregates \texttt  {SimResult[T$^2$]} into a \texttt  {TileReduction} ($\sim $80 bytes), which is the \emph  {only} data crossing the GPU$\to $CPU bus. The CPU scheduler reads it to make split/priority decisions. The rendering path (GPU$\to $GPU) is unchanged from Layers\nobreakspace  {}0--1.}}{73}{figure.0.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dataflow_layer2}{{28}{73}{Layer~2 data flow. The GPU reduction pass aggregates \texttt {SimResult[T$^2$]} into a \texttt {TileReduction} ($\sim $80 bytes), which is the \emph {only} data crossing the GPU$\to $CPU bus. The CPU scheduler reads it to make split/priority decisions. The rendering path (GPU$\to $GPU) is unchanged from Layers~0--1}{figure.0.28}{}}
